# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is speed: node_modules and .git are most of this
# repo's bytes and the image needs neither (the builder runs `npm ci` from the
# lockfile, which is the only reproducible way to get a tree anyway).
#
# The one that matters more: KEEPING A DEVELOPER'S LAPTOP OUT OF THE IMAGE.
# `packages/web/dist` is a build artifact that is gitignored precisely because
# it is whatever the last local `npm run dev` left behind; if it rode into the
# build context it would be COPY'd over the freshly built bundle and the image
# would serve a stale canvas that matched no commit. Same for `.isocan/`, which
# holds this machine's agent identity, and `.env*`, which holds whatever
# somebody once pasted there.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image, never imported into it.
packages/web/dist
dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# Local state and scratch.
.isocan
scratch
.claude
.agents
*.log
.DS_Store

# Secrets, in the two shapes they usually arrive in.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*-key.json
*credentials*.json

# Things that describe the repo rather than run it. Excluded so a docs-only
# commit reuses every layer — the `COPY . .` above `npm run build` is what
# would otherwise be invalidated by a typo fix in a markdown file.
#
# NOT excluded, deliberately: package.json (the version /healthz reports),
# the tsconfigs, and packages/cli/src/agent-guide.md — the CLI's own test
# reads that file, and a shipped daemon that could not produce it would be a
# daemon whose --agent-help is a lie.
LICENSE
README.md
AGENTS.md
docs
test
**/test
vitest.config.ts

# Per-package `scripts/` directories are DEV TOOLS, and one of them is a tool
# that talks to a real bucket: packages/cloudstore/scripts/signed-url-smoke.ts.
# Nothing imports it, so shipping it would be inert rather than dangerous — but
# an operator smoke-testing signatures is not a thing the home does, and a file
# in an image is a file somebody eventually runs. Out.
#
# The ROOT `scripts/` stays: package.json's `prepare` names scripts/prepare.mjs,
# and a manifest pointing at a file that is not there is a trap for any npm
# command in the image that decides to run a lifecycle hook.
packages/*/scripts
